            <td>60 minutes</td>
          </tr>

          <tr>
            <td>Technical Subjects</td>
            <td>60 minutes</td>
          </tr>

          <tr>
            <td>Communication</td>
            <td>30 minutes</td>
          </tr>

          <tr>
            <td>Interview Practice</td>
            <td>30 minutes</td>
          </tr>

        </table>

        <div class="info-box">

          <strong>Remember:</strong>
          Consistent daily practice is more useful than studying
          everything at the last minute.

        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- FAQ -->
      <section class="content-section" id="faq">

        <h2>14. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <div class="faq">

          <h3>1. When should I start placement preparation?</h3>

          <p>
            It is better to start early during college. Starting early
            gives enough time to improve coding, aptitude, technical
            knowledge and communication skills.
          </p>


          <h3>2. Is coding necessary for software jobs?</h3>

          <p>
            Many software roles require programming and problem-solving
            skills. The exact coding requirements depend on the company
            and job role.
          </p>


          <h3>3. Which programming language should I learn?</h3>

          <p>
            Choose one programming language and learn its fundamentals
            properly. Java, Python and C++ are commonly used for
            programming practice.
          </p>


          <h3>4. How can I improve my aptitude?</h3>

          <p>
            Learn the basic formulas, understand different problem types
            and solve questions regularly with a time limit.
          </p>


          <h3>5. How can I improve my interview skills?</h3>

          <p>
            Practice common technical and HR questions, participate in
            mock interviews and improve your communication skills.
          </p>


          <h3>6. How important is a resume?</h3>

          <p>
            A resume helps recruiters understand your education, skills,
            projects and experience. It should be accurate, clear and
            relevant to the position.
          </p>


          <h3>7. What should I do before a technical interview?</h3>

          <p>
            Revise programming, data structures, DBMS, SQL, operating
            systems, computer networks and the technical subjects
            relevant to the job.
          </p>


          <h3>8. How can I become confident in interviews?</h3>

          <p>
            Confidence improves through preparation and practice.
            Practice speaking clearly, review common questions and
            participate in mock interviews.
          </p>

        </div>

      </section>


